  "summary": "Augusta County Sheriff Donald Smith issued a statement defending the sheriff's office's use of two Flock cameras on Jefferson Highway, citing their use in a homicide investigation, stolen vehicle recoveries, and missing-person cases. Smith acknowledged privacy concerns amid other Valley localities discontinuing Flock use, and said access to the system is controlled, logged, and audited, and that he will continue reviewing usage.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "access to the system is strictly controlled, monitored, and logged",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    },
    {
      "quote": "Augusta County is a large community with limited law enforcement resources, and technology like Flock cameras can help investigators work cases more efficiently",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    }
